1
00:00:00,400 --> 00:00:05,900
This is Iron Chef, a small app I built in Python. I copy a recipe from a web page, paste it into my own form, and one click saves it as a Word document.

2
00:00:06,400 --> 00:00:11,200
On the left, the app I built: an empty form. On the right, a recipe web page I'll copy from.

3
00:00:11,600 --> 00:00:17,200
First, the basics. I type in the recipe's name, where it came from, and how long it takes.

4
00:00:17,600 --> 00:00:23,200
Next, the nutrition facts. I copy them from the web page and paste them into the form.

5
00:00:23,600 --> 00:00:28,200
Then the ingredients, copied over the same way.

6
00:00:28,600 --> 00:00:32,700
And the five cooking steps go into the Instructions box.

7
00:00:33,100 --> 00:00:39,700
Now, the one click: Save Recipe. A pop-up confirms it worked, and a new file appears in the project.

8
00:00:40,100 --> 00:00:50,700
Here's that file. The recipe is now a Word document, with its title, source, cook time, nutrition facts, ingredients, and directions.

9
00:00:51,100 --> 00:00:58,000
Six details from a web page, one click, one saved document. That's the whole app.

